"25kembyp2yg": "The ledger has no names, only the first syllable of the neighborhood and a number. Si = Sijang (the Central Market), Mok = Mokgol, Sang = Sangpo-dong.",
"1dlp9rph7ee": "※ The ledger contains no list linking the numbers to people. The complainant says it is “in my head.” (So)",
"29k3frztac4": "Investigation Diary (So Byeong-guk) — 2",
"pd43muz8oc": "Nov 27, 1986 – Jan 10, 1987 · pencil",
"wuxw5q4wwz": "Nov 27 Han Jeong-mi, waitress at the Celadon Tearoom. Says Pyeon wrote numbers on the inside of a matchbox before he made his calls that night. The matchbox is waterlogged, the writing smeared. Asked the forensics unit for [[infrared photography|k_ir]].",
"20o0n0eez8i": "Dec 3 Reply from forensics. The ballpoint marks came up under infrared, they say. Three prints. Lookup tomorrow.",
"1p1n0nwnf7s": "Dec 4 Section chief: “Forget the lookup and shore up the butcher case.” Woo's already been let go, and he wants it shored up.",
"1f4b1ao1gei": "Dec 11 Half a day canvassing Mokgol. The night watchman at the sawmill by the ferry looks like he knows something, but he keeps his mouth shut.",
"156xhvbzfhq": "Dec 20 Task force scaled down. I'm off to traffic.",
"eo797oud42": "Jan 10 Task force disbanded. Tucking the three matchbox prints, envelope and all, into the back of the file. In case someone looks.",
